		{
			dependencies: ["2645C1A262AC779D"]
			description: [
				"Smelting the tiny dusts you get from surface vein indicators, you can get some copper nuggets and then crudely forge them into proper ingots."
				""
				"&2DON'T PANIC!&r The terrible smelting ratios (as well as the walking around in search for tiny piles) will only be around for a short while, after which you'll be able to make a furnace and refine all metals as if you're playing vanilla."
				""
				""
				"{@pagebreak}"
				"Iron is objectively better than copper when it comes to tools. For this reason, you might want to gather up enough copper for some mining hammers, 8 or so furnaces and a bunch extra just in case, after which you can set up a proper base on one of the iron veins."
			]
			id: "63361EFFEE5FAE29"
			subtitle: "How many ores per ingot?!"
			tasks: [
				{
					id: "14CCD890139433D0"
